  "versionCode": 104,
  "versionName": "3.1.8",
  "notes": "Bannerlator 3.1.8: move a game to another container; GOG prerequisites install from Windows components without opening the container; Visual C++ with MFC that really installs; GOG fixes (games that restart themselves, sign-in check, download progress); Xbox libraries that stayed empty.",
  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Move a game",
      "text": "Move a game to another container from its settings, with its saves, files and the components it needs."
    },
    {
      "title": "GOG prerequisites",
      "text": "A GOG game's Visual C++, DirectX and .NET install from Windows components, without opening the container."
    },
    {
      "title": "Visual C++",
      "text": "Includes MFC now, and only counts as installed when Microsoft's files are really in the container."
    },
    {
      "title": "GOG fixes",
      "text": "Games that restart themselves stay open, sign-in passes the \"I'm human\" check, and downloads show real progress."
    }
  ],
